    "title": "Justin Rose career earnings: Breaking down how much money former U.S. Open winner has made, net worth | Sporting News",
    "text": "Justin Rose turned professional in 1998. He was born in Johannesburg, South Africa but moved to England when he was five. Rose began playing golf at an early age and reportedly broke 70 for the first time when he was 11. He was one of the most highly anticipated golfers coming to the PGA Tour in the early 2000s. Rose played a PGA Tour major for the first time at the 2002 PGA Championship when he finished tied for 23rd. Rose won the 2013 U.S. Open, and it remains his only PGA Tour major championship victory. He has finished in second at the Masters twice, one as a tie in 2015 and once outright in 2017. Rose has also finished second at the Open Championship (2018, 2024), and his best finish at the PGA Championship is a tie for third in 2012.📲 Follow The Sporting News on WhatsApp With a 27-year career under his belt, here is how much money Rose has made as a professional golfer. Justin Rose career earningsAccording to Spotrac, Rose has earned $58,642,758 on the PGA Tour and an additional $13,609,504 from playing in majors, for a total of $72,252,262. While Rose has only one major championship, he has 11 wins on the European Tour. His best year came in 2018, when he earned $6,967,152. That year, he won the Fort Worth Invitational, came in second at the BMW Championship, won the Turkish Airlines Open, finished tied for second at the Open Championship and tied for 10th at the U.S. Open. SN's MASTERS HQ: Live Masters leaderboard | Masters TV coverage | Live streamingJustin Rose net worthAccording to Celebrity Net Worth, Rose has a net worth of $40 million. In addition to his outright winnings from golf tournaments, Rose has plenty of sponsorships and endorsement deals in the golf world that contribute to his net worth. He is still searching for his second major win, and his first in over 10 years. When Rose accomplishes that, we will be in for a nice payday. MORE TO KNOW ABOUT THE MASTERSCan you play Augusta National? Inside the exclusive golf club’s membership rulesEverything you need to know about the coveted Masters Green JacketScottie Scheffler at the Masters: A complete record of his results and performances",
